Here's the working program (`Program.cs`):

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions { PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase };
var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new Person("Jane", 30), options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string Name, int Age);
```

It targets `net8.0` and outputs `{"name":"Jane","age":30}` as expected. The key is setting `PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase` on `JsonSerializerOptions` — this converts PascalCase properties (`Name`, `Age`) to camelCase (`name`, `age`) during serialization.
